DESCRIPTION:This French-language performance (with English subtitles) bri
 ngs to life Michel Foucault's celebrated 1970 inaugural lecture for which
  no recording survives. The questions it raises for education\, freedom o
 f speech\, and our daily lives feel more urgent than ever. A Théâtre na
 tional Bordeaux Aquitaine production\, the performance at IU Bloomington 
 makes only one of the two U.S. stops during Foucault's centenary year.  P
 erformance\, followed by a discussion with the audience
