SUMMARY:Level Up Your Global Impact: Peace Corps Virtual Info Session & Q&A
DESCRIPTION:Tired of the usual career tracks and ready to actually make a
  tangible difference on the ground?  Join the HLS Office of Policy Engage
 ment and Strategic Partnerships and Peace Corps Regional Recruiter Clauda
 le Daniels for an interactive\, zero-BS virtual info session and Q&amp\;A
 . Forget traditional desk jobs—we're talking about on-the-ground immers
 ion where you learn a new language\, integrate into a local community\, a
 nd tackle real-world challenges side-by-side with global partners.  Wheth
 er you're passionate about international development\, education\, enviro
 nmental action\, or public service\, we'll break down:The Real Experience
 : What daily life\, cultural integration\, and grassroots collaboration a
 ctually look like in the field.    Choose Your Path: Exploring traditiona
 l 2-year global service\, flexible Peace Corps Response projects\, and th
 e Virtual Service Pilot.    The Long Game: How stepping into the world po
 st-graduation builds the kind of cross-cultural leadership\, grit\, and g
 lobal network that sets you apart in any career—plus paths like the Cov
 erdale Fellowship and federal career benefits.      Bring your questions\
 , grab your coffee\, and find out how to take your global ambitions off t
 he screen and into the real world before Claudale visits IU's campus in p
 erson later this spring! Meeting URL: https://iu.zoom.us/my/hlspesp
